id: pm-vcs-8qyx
title: Bound manifest metadata so a fragmented file's memory ceiling does not scale with its length
description: "A fragment manifest holds one entry per fragment, so its size grows with totalLength divided by fragmentSize. writeFragmentedFile retains every entry and returns the whole manifest, encodeManifest builds all lines into one buffer, and decodeManifest splits the full payload and retains every entry. The content path is genuinely streaming after the corrected proofs, but the metadata path is not, so the fixed memory ceiling the feature promises does not hold at the top of the size range. At the 1 MiB default fragment size a 1 GiB file is about 1024 entries, which is unremarkable, and a 1 TiB file is about a million entries, which is not. The likely shape is a multi-level manifest so a reader touches only the entries covering the range it asked for, which is also what makes a range read on a very large file cheap."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: fragments,memory,scale
created_at: "2026-09-08T17:34:52.473Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T09:36:58.602Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "Peak metadata memory for a read and for a range read is bounded independently of totalLength, proven the same way the content proofs are: sample while the operation is in flight and fail against an implementation that materializes every entry; encode and decode do not require the whole manifest resident; existing manifests remain readable"
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:35:49.174Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — content streaming is implemented (engine/fragments.ts: writeFragmentedFile reads the source in bounded chunks, peak heap bounded by fragmentSize). Range reads touch only overlapping fragments (test/fragments.test.ts). REMAINS — the manifest metadata path is NOT bounded independently of totalLength: writeFragmentedFile materializes the full manifest entry list (line 158: peak heap bounded by fragmentSize plus the manifest entry list), encodeManifest builds all lines into one buffer, and decodeManifest splits the full payload. No multi-level manifest exists (grep for multi-level/level manifest returns no matches). A 1 TiB file at 1 MiB fragments would produce about a million manifest entries, all resident. The acceptance criteria require peak metadata memory bounded independently of totalLength and encode/decode not requiring the whole manifest resident."
  "2026-10-11T05:07:26.998Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator confirmed the current streaming content path retains a full fragment metadata array. The implementation will bound manifest metadata for write, read and range operations, retain legacy readability, and add a measured regression with behavioral revert evidence at unchanged coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T05:11:21.877Z",codex-sol,"Plan: bounded-fanout canonical manifest nodes with incremental writer and range-seeking traversal, legacy v1 reads, and closure/bundle/erasure integration. Measure live metadata retention on real fragmented files and record focused pass, behavioral revert failure and restored pass at unchanged coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T05:14:25.937Z",codex-agent,"Independent design review: the bounded format must prove streaming writer and read/range behavior while operations are in flight, with unchanged production functions reverted. Check retained legacy v1 reads explicitly: decoding a large v1 object into its full entry array remains a metadata growth path, so either bound that reader too or make the legacy compatibility boundary explicit and verify it against the written acceptance criteria. Also exercise height/count/length validation and closure, bundle and erasure behavior for interior nodes."
  "2026-10-11T05:25:55.574Z",codex-agent,"Independent review requested a stronger measurement before full gates: counting entries in each individual physical node cannot detect a reader retaining all nodes or flattening all entries. Read and range regressions must also fail for behaviorally correct full-list materialization, and large legacy v1 read behavior must satisfy the stated metadata bound."
  "2026-10-11T05:32:02.196Z",codex-sol,"Review correction: per-node entry counts alone do not prove live retention. Added separate real 48 MiB heap children over 1,048,577 logical fragments for full read and range, for both paged and legacy v1 metadata. Legacy compatibility now uses a backpressured decompression worker and bounded canonical line traversal while preserving synchronous callers. Behavioral full-list reverts will be measured separately."
  "2026-10-11T05:42:39.434Z",codex-agent,"Independent orchestrator verification: node --expose-gc --test test/manifest-memory.test.ts passed 2/2 with zero skips and four real 48 MiB heap children over 1048577 logical fragments. Sampled live heap was 26705184 and 26791368 bytes for legacy read/range, and 26724352 and 26649552 bytes for paged read/range. Separate native-source and compiled Node/Bun probes confirmed a zero-length range rejects a tampered large legacy object. Full-list behavioral reverts and exact-head release gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-11T05:50:13.910Z",codex-sol,"Measured real filesystem baseline PASS: two format scenarios, each exercising full read and tail range in separate 48 MiB heap children over 1,048,577 logical fragments. In-flight live heap bytes: v1 read 26706392, v1 range 26808808, paged read 26711864, paged range 26641632. No skipped tests. Replaced range result-parts retention with direct copies into the requested output buffer. Legacy compatibility now verifies the entire canonical line stream and enclosing object hash under bounded decompression/backpressure. Correct-output full-list reader reverts and original writer revert are next."
  "2026-10-11T06:04:02.499Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral proof: changing only readFragmentedToFile to obtain materializeManifest(store, id), then traversing its flat logical fragments with the unchanged correct output code, failed the paged 48 MiB heap child with SIGABRT and FATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit. Changing only readFragmentRange the same way also exhausted the unchanged heap; its full-read control passed at 26711544 live heap bytes. Restoring only the original writeFragmentedFile implementation failed the unchanged measured node bound with 32769 resident serialized entries versus 128. The first writer revert attempt had an invalid helper import and is not counted as behavioral evidence; a corrected import and isolated function restoration produced the measured failure. Native TypeScript imports required no dist rebuild for these proofs. Restored complete focused suites and gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-11T06:23:39.964Z",codex-sol,"Restored PASS evidence: node --expose-gc --test test/manifest-memory.test.ts executed under c8 collection with two passing format scenarios, zero skipped. Four independent 48 MiB children measured live heap bytes v1 read 28721608, v1 range 28816520, paged read 28705560, paged range 28648600 over 1048577 logical entries. Restored focused coverage execution passed 35/35 tests, zero skipped. Baseline full-suite exploration was stopped after an existing readiness wait failed to reject a timed-out child; the wait now rejects process exit without changing its deadline. Additional CLI fixture lease lifetime is being made appropriate for multiple real process startups; explicit expiry tests remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T06:41:19.865Z",codex-sol,"Required linked execution passed: pm test pm-vcs-8qyx --run --progress ran node --expose-gc --test test/manifest-pages.test.ts test/manifest-memory.test.ts test/feature-edges.test.ts, 29/29 passed, zero failed, cancelled, skipped or todo; exit 0. In-flight live heap bytes over 1048577 fragments: legacy read 26720720, legacy range 26807176, paged read 26727504, paged range 26672784, each in a separate 48 MiB child. Original-writer and correct-content materializing-reader revert failures plus restored PASS remain recorded. Full unchanged coverage gate remains underway."
  "2026-10-11T07:02:00.113Z",codex-sol,"The interrupted full coverage exploration is incomplete evidence, not a gate pass. Raw coverage data and external logs are preserved. Test fixture startup and serial CLI watchdogs are being corrected for shared CPU contention; measured 48 MiB heap budgets, materialization regressions, production deadlines, coverage thresholds and source inventory remain unchanged. Isolated failing cases precede fresh complete coverage and committed-HEAD gates."
  "2026-10-11T07:15:15.225Z",codex-agent,"Independent review completed the full-buffer convenience reader as well: readFragmented now copies each logical fragment directly into its single requested result buffer, removing the Buffer handle array that scaled with fragment count. Its full content allocation remains explicit; metadata and live fragment payload retention stay bounded. Streaming file/range heap budgets and behavioral proofs are unchanged. This small source refinement was made during an exploratory coverage run; committed-HEAD release gates must verify the final integrated source."
  "2026-10-11T07:16:46.651Z",codex-agent,"Independent fragment/page suite found a real empty-range regression: 60/61 passed, but a zero-length interval inside a fragment still selected that blob after the legacy-validation early return was removed. Corrected manifest traversal so bounded nodes return no entries for empty intervals; large legacy streams still verify all canonical metadata and the enclosing hash, but yield no fragment for an empty interval. Existing no-blob-read assertion remains unchanged. A restored 61-case rerun is underway; final HEAD gates must include this refinement and the direct-copy full-buffer reader."
  "2026-10-11T07:19:56.570Z",codex-agent,"Independent restored reader/page verification: node --expose-gc --test test/fragments.test.ts test/manifest-pages.test.ts passed 61/61, zero failures, cancellations or skips. This includes the unchanged no-blob-read assertion for an empty interval, direct-copy full-buffer convenience reads, streamed file/range behavior, paged closure and legacy compatibility. An intermediate run without the repository-required expose-gc setting had a noisy buffer-memory sample and is not the restored gate evidence. Final committed-HEAD gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-11T07:48:28.998Z",codex-agent,"The raw coverage guard failure was its explicit source-count assertion, not an ignore directive: five new production modules increase the inventory from 53 to 58. Updated the expected count to 58; the complete root/engine/scripts glob and the prohibition on coverage ignore directives are unchanged. Coverage thresholds remain 100 percent in every metric."
  "2026-10-11T07:55:36.098Z",codex-sol,"After publication metadata reuse, the linked command node --expose-gc --test test/manifest-pages.test.ts test/manifest-memory.test.ts test/feature-edges.test.ts passed again through pm test --run --progress: 29/29, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo. The unchanged bounded-heap children retain legacy and paged full/range coverage. Source and test typecheck, lint, duplicate detection (58 source files, zero clones), and docstrings (327 declarations) pass. The surviving diagnostic full run is being collected before final complete gates."
  "2026-10-11T07:58:04.803Z",codex-agent,"Independent source inventory verification: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"production coverage contains no ignore directives\" test/raw-coverage.test.ts passed 1/1 with no skips. All 58 production sources are included and none carries a coverage ignore directive; thresholds remain 100 percent."
  "2026-10-11T08:11:43.048Z",codex-sol,"Final linked execution after receiver-boundary assertions and finite manifest finalization passed node --expose-gc --test test/manifest-pages.test.ts test/manifest-memory.test.ts test/feature-edges.test.ts through pm test pm-vcs-8qyx --run --progress: 30/30, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo, exit 0. Fanout 128, bounded hierarchy and 48 MiB heap children are unchanged; legacy compatibility still verifies every canonical row and full object hash. Correct-output full-list read/range reverts and original writer revert remain recorded with restored PASS. The fresh complete unchanged 100 percent coverage gate is pending."
  "2026-10-11T09:03:15.164Z",codex-sol,"Complete unchanged npm run coverage passed 1419/1419 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, and 100/100/100/100 statements/branches/functions/lines across all 58 production files. Final linked pm test --run --progress passed 31/31 manifest/heap/edge tests, zero skips. Streaming disk and buffer writers use fanout-128 authenticated hierarchies; full/range readers use bounded traversal and verified bounded v1 decompression. Convenience full-buffer/manifest contracts explicitly materialize only on request. Real 48 MiB children over 1048577 fragmented entries pass both formats and both read operations. Correct-content reverts changing only full read or only range read to materializeManifest(...).fragments each failed with heap exhaustion; restoring only the original disk writer failed with 32769 serialized entries versus bound 128. Restored focused tests and complete coverage pass. Canonical identity, malformed structures, closure, instances, erasure, bundle and transport compatibility are covered. Legacy v1 range verification scans all metadata for integrity and has linear time but bounded memory. Releasing the claim while keeping this item in_progress/open. Changelog, self-host bundle and committed-HEAD npm/Bun/isolated-identity gates are next; final gate counts will be reported without another tracker write."
  "2026-10-11T09:26:14.769Z",codex-agent,"The first committed npm release gate reported 1418 of 1419 tests passing, with zero cancellations, skips or todo. The streaming read buffer sample was 131279 bytes against its unchanged 131072-byte ceiling on a 524288-byte file. The case passed alone and all 55 fragment tests passed under coverage, identifying insufficient margin in the new fixed output buffer. Reduced the production output buffer from 64 KiB to 32 KiB; metadata paging, fragment payload limits, the 48 MiB child heaps and every test assertion remain unchanged. Re-running linked feature tests and all three release gates at a new frozen commit."
  "2026-10-11T09:35:14.889Z",codex-sol,"The first committed-HEAD npm release gate at 066da5e completed 1419 tests: 1418 passed, one failed, zero cancellations/skips/todo; all production coverage remained 100/100/100/100. The existing restore buffer assertion observed 131279 bytes against the unchanged strict bound 131072 (512 KiB file / 4), a 207-byte overrun. Native and covered isolated checks passed, and all 55 fragment tests passed under coverage; reduced the actual output coalescing allocation from 64 KiB to 32 KiB to leave buffer headroom without changing any assertion, heap budget, production deadline or source inventory. Documented the actual allocation. Covered focused run passed 80/80; refreshed linked PM runs passed manifest/heap/edge 31/31, fragment suite 55/55 and combined restore/edge/heap 80/80, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo. Existing correct-content materialization reverts still fail before output-buffer allocation; original writer and preflight-only proofs are unchanged. Source/test typecheck, lint, zero duplicates and 327 docstrings pass. Releasing claims again before changelog and bundle regeneration; the corrected HEAD will receive all three complete release gates."
  "2026-10-11T09:36:49.420Z",codex-agent,"The 32 KiB output buffer passed both tracker-linked commands: manifest/pages/heap/boundaries 31 of 31 and fragment regressions 55 of 55, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo. The unchanged 128-entry node bound and all four 48 MiB reader children passed. Correct-output materialization revert proofs are unchanged. Candidate, package validation receipts and review are tracked in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/100; npm, Bun and isolated Git-identity gates will use the frozen refined commit."
